# gemiprint — Cursor Agent Rules

## Owner context

- The owner is **not a programmer**. Trust technical decisions to the agent; explain changes briefly in plain Bahasa Indonesia.
- Internal app, ~2-5 users. Priorities: fast, stable, fits business needs, reasonable security (not enterprise hardening).
- Communicate with the owner in **Bahasa Indonesia**.

## Workflow

- Treat each request as a **goal to finish end-to-end**, not a question to answer. Implement UI + logic + data, fix compile errors you introduce, then verify.
- Don't pause for unnecessary check-ins ("should I continue?"). Proceed unless truly blocked.
- `/goal <text>` mode: everything after `/goal` is the single goal. Ship the behavior first, then test/cleanup. Don't stop at a plan.
- Pick reasonable defaults for small ambiguities; note assumptions in the final summary.
- **Block and ask only if:** deleting production data / wiping DB, changing domain/DNS/billing, money or access rules that can't be inferred, or changes that can't be rolled back easily.

## Tools and access (use without asking)

- Cursor built-in browser (GitHub, Supabase, Vercel, GoDaddy — already logged in).
- Terminal / CLI: Next.js, Flutter, `gh`, Supabase CLI, Vercel CLI, SQLite.
- Read code, run commands, check deploy/logs, test in the browser.

## Git and deploy

- Commit verified changes. Push to `main` → Vercel auto-deploys.
- Only commit when the owner asks (or clearly implies). Clear commit messages.
- Never commit secrets (`.env.local`, keys, certs). Never `git push --force` to `main`. Don't amend pushed commits unless asked.
- DB migrations: after pushing schema changes, the owner runs `npm run supabase:db:push` to apply to cloud.

## Architecture (one app, three storage backends)

- **Web** (`app.gemiprint.com`, Vercel): React + Next.js API routes → Supabase Postgres via service-role key.
- **Desktop** (Tauri + Next standalone): local SQLite via `better-sqlite3`, offline-first, optional sync to Supabase. Entry: `src-tauri/src/main.rs`; sync engine: `src-tauri/src/sync.rs`.
- **Mobile / mobile-web** (Flutter): talks only to the Next.js API.
- **Unified data layer:** `src/lib/db-unified.ts`. Use `db.query/queryOne/insert/update/delete/transaction`. **Never import the Supabase or SQLite client directly from feature code.**
- **Runtime:** Node.js 22 + npm. Stay on it.

### File map by concern

- DB access (all backends): `src/lib/db-unified.ts`
- Stock movements + roll conversion: `src/lib/services/inventory-service.ts` (`postInventoryMovement`, `convertRollVariant`)
- Cashbook + AVCO: `src/lib/services/finance-service.ts`
- Auth guards: `src/lib/auth-guard-server.ts`
- Period close: `src/lib/services/accounting-periods-service.ts`
- PPN helpers: `src/lib/ppn-helpers.ts`; roll billing: `src/lib/roll-size-utils.ts`
- Cache hook: `src/lib/use-cached-data.ts`; sync table list: `src/lib/sync-config.ts`
- Menu + breadcrumb: `src/components/menuConfig.tsx`

## Language standard (Indonesia-first)

The whole app is normalized to Bahasa Indonesia. All application-owned artifacts use Indonesian: UI strings, route folders, API routes, component names, comments/JSDoc, internal docs, internal scripts, and new DB tables/columns.

**English is only allowed for** framework/library/protocol terms and fixed names: `src`, `page.tsx`, `route.ts`, React props, SQL keywords, npm package names, built-in types (`string`, `Promise`, `Record`, ...), generated/vendor code, and migrations already applied to cloud.

**Conventions still in force (do not regress):**

- New comments/JSDoc in touched application code must be Bahasa Indonesia. When you touch a nearby English app comment, translate it (keep the edit scoped). Don't translate framework/generated/vendor comments.
- Use baku Indonesian spelling, not half-English: Impor (not Import), Ekspor (not Export), Unggah (not Upload), Unduh (not Download), Muat Ulang (not Refresh), Pratinjau (not Preview), Penggantian (not Override), Bawaan / Utama (not Default), Buat (not Generate), Draf (not Draft), Jendela (not Window), Faktur (not Invoice), Pelanggan Umum (not Walk-in), Manajer/Staf (not Manager/Staff).
- Don't abbreviate operational menu labels: "PO" → "Pesanan Pembelian", "SJ" → "Surat Jalan". "SPK", "PPN", "NSFP", "POS", "maklon", "finishing", "Vendor" stay (baku operational terms).
- Don't add new bilingual (i18n) toggles for internal UI. Exception that exists: AI design-brief generator in `src/app/produksi/ai-prompt/page.tsx` (consumed by outside vendors).
- Glossary: Dashboard→Beranda, Customer→Pelanggan, Material→Barang, Purchase→Pembelian, Sale→Penjualan, Inventory→Inventori, Finance→Keuangan, Reports→Laporan, Settings→Pengaturan, User→Pengguna, Production→Produksi.

**Deployed-contract safety:** never rename a deployed DB column / API path casually. Add a new migration (additive) or a compat alias, migrate consumers, verify, then remove the old one. DB rename must stay in sync across Supabase migration, `database/sqlite-schema.sql`, `src/lib/db-unified.ts` runtime ALTER, `src/lib/sync-config.ts`, services, web, Tauri, and Flutter.

**Settled exceptions (kept English on purpose):**
- File names under `src/lib/services/*-service.ts` and `src/lib/*.ts` may stay English (read by programmers; renaming churns every import for no user value).
- Legacy DB tables already in English (`inventory_movements`, `purchase_orders`, `stock_opnames`, `barang_roll_variants`, `accounting_periods`, ...) stay — renaming tables is high-risk (many FKs) for low value. New tables/columns must be Indonesian.
- Old API folders under `src/app/api/` (e.g. `/api/customers`) are kept as thin re-export shims pointing at the Indonesian routes (`/api/pelanggan`) until Flutter/Tauri migrate. Old web routes (`/customers`, `/dashboard`, ...) 301-redirect to Indonesian routes via `next.config.ts`.

## Iron rules — data & money (apply unprompted)

The owner won't remember to ask; enforce by default.

1. **Data fetching → `useCachedData` (SWR), never `useAsyncData`.** Instant paint from cache + background revalidate. Stable cache key per dataset (e.g. `"pelanggan"`, or `` `movement-ledger:${JSON.stringify(filters)}` ``). Bust cross-page caches with `useInvalidate("key")`. Reference: `src/app/barang/page.tsx`, `src/app/vendors/page.tsx`.

2. **Schema change → THREE places in sync:** (a) new `supabase/migrations/<timestamp>_<name>.sql` (additive, `IF NOT EXISTS`, defaults); (b) `database/sqlite-schema.sql` fresh-install template; (c) `src/lib/db-unified.ts` runtime `ALTER TABLE ADD COLUMN` so existing SQLite installs migrate on start. Migrations already on cloud are immutable — write a new one.

3. **Inventory mutation → `inventory-service.postInventoryMovement`, never raw `db.update("barang", { jumlah_stok })`.** The ledger `inventory_movements` is the source of truth for stock + AVCO. Roll cuts use `convertRollVariant`. Rebuild via `rebuildInventoryBalance(barangId)`.

4. **Money/cashbook mutation → `keuangan` with a `[REF:<id>]` token in `keperluan`.** Void/revert search this token. Hutang/piutang flow through `payDebt` / `revertDebtPayment`; keep `keuangan`, `hutang.sisa_hutang`, `pembelian.jumlah_dibayar` in lock-step. CASH posts to `keuangan` immediately; NET30/COD creates `hutang` and posts only when paid.

5. **Mutating server action → wrap in an auth guard** (`src/lib/auth-guard-server.ts`: `requireSession`, `requireAdminOrManager`, `requireProductionInventoryRole`, `requireAdminManagerOrSelf`). Pass `session.uid` as `dibuat_oleh`. Read actions can be ungated.

6. **Roll/dimensional barang (`butuh_dimensi_status = 1`):** `jumlah` (m²) = `jumlah_roll × panjang × lebar` (never just `panjang × lebar`). Decrement uses roll-width-aligned length via `barang_roll_variants` + `linear_delta_m`. Conversions atomic + AVCO-neutral. Input order **Lebar × Panjang**. Roll qty integer ≥ 1.

7. **Period-closed guard on dated mutations.** Anything accepting `tanggal` must check `accounting-periods-service.isDateInClosedPeriod`. Throw a friendly error pointing to the open period; never silently bypass.

8. **Sync columns on every new synced table:** `sync_status, last_synced_at, sync_version, updated_at_server, updated_by_device, change_version, is_deleted, deleted_at, client_mutation_id`. Register it in `src/lib/sync-config.ts`.

9. **Idempotent ledger IDs from source line:** `mov-${itemId}`, `void-${originalMovementId}`, `${conversionId}-out` / `${conversionId}-in-${i}`. Deterministic and retry-safe.

10. **Verification before "done" (mandatory):** `npm run type-check` (0 errors) → `npm run build` → `npx jest <relevant test>` for touched services (`src/lib/__tests__/`). UI-only changes may skip jest, still need type-check + build. New lint warnings you introduce must be fixed.

11. **`onSuccess` for a newly created item passes `null` as the updated item**, so the parent does a full `reload()` instead of `updateInState` (which would never append the new row).

12. **Seed/default SQL:** verify column names against actual migrations (e.g. `pengaturan_toko` bank fields are `bank_nama`, `bank_nomor`, `bank_atas_nama`). Default settings rows use `ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE SET`, not `DO NOTHING`, so `supabase:local:reset` restores defaults.

13. **Finance categories:** show `display_name` as primary label; `category_code` secondary (small, monospace, amber, quoted). In `ExpressionAssistant`, suggestion `label` = display name, `hint` = `kode: ${code}`, `insert` = `"${code}"`.

## Iron rules — new page/UI shape

- Page root is `<div className="space-y-6">`, **never** a second `<main>` (the shell already provides `<main>` with padding).
- Every page opens with a gradient title card: `<div className="bg-gradient-to-br from-X to-Y rounded-2xl shadow-lg p-6 text-white">` with icon, uppercase title, subtitle. Reference: `src/app/keuangan/page.tsx`, `src/app/surat-jalan/page.tsx`.
- **Dark mode mandatory on every element.** Every color class needs a `dark:` pair (`bg-white dark:bg-slate-900`, `text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-100`, `border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700`). Watch for invalid tokens like `dark:bg-slate-8000`.
- Stat-card icons use `text-white` on a `bg-white/20 rounded-lg` patch — never the same color as the card gradient (invisible icon).
- Badges/numbers with white text need a solid shade (`bg-emerald-500`), not `-50` (near-white, unreadable).
- **Modals:** ESC to close, backdrop click to close (`if (e.target === e.currentTarget)`), header X button, primary action rightmost with brand color, cancel to its left, disabled state during async ("Menyimpan..."). Theme color by domain: emerald = material/inventory, purple = purchase, indigo = neutral, amber = warnings/manual, rose = destructive. Reference shells: `src/components/ModalFormShell.tsx`, `src/components/DialogKonfirmasi.tsx`.

## When ambiguous

Pick the option that: matches existing patterns (search first), minimizes new infra, errs toward user safety on destructive ops, and respects existing column/table semantics. Document non-obvious choices in the final summary.

## Setup references (owner-maintained, do not delete)

- `docs/SETUP.md` — fresh-machine developer setup.
- `docs/supabase-local-development.md` — local Supabase workflow.
